# A Killer Among Us: each copy has its own choice, the same or not (ruling 2024-02-02; CR 607.2d). Bot1 casts one on turn 1 and
# chooses Human; on turn 3 casts a second (Ancient Tomb and three Moxen) and chooses Goblin. Both enchantments are then on the
# battlefield with their own choice. The turn 1 tokens attack (the turn 3 ones are summoning sick): the first copy (Human) is
# revealed on the Human token and the second (Goblin) on the Goblin token, each giving its own type's token +3/+3; the Merfolk,
# which neither names, stays 1/1.

